diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a1c7bd..7b23371 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -56,12 +56,20 @@ after each text block.
 %{R}                         Swap background and foreground colors
 %{O:[0xRRGGBB[AA]:size]}     Overline color:size in pixel
 %{U:[0xRRGGBB[AA]:size]}     Underline color:size in pixel
-%{X:size}                    Offset in pixel in the alignment direction
+%{X:size}                    Offset in logical pixels in the alignment direction
+%{G:size}                    Minimum logical-pixel gap before the right group
 %{A:action}                  Text to send to the STDOUT on mouse click
 %{l|c|r}                     Alignment of the text (left|center|right) in
                                the bar
 ```

+`%{G:size}` applies to the right-aligned group containing the following text
+block. The largest gap declared by entries in that group is used. Without
+`%{G}`, the gap is zero. Zelbar computes the right group's start and clips the
+left group at whole-glyph boundaries. Truncated text ends with one `…`; fully
+visible text does not. The gap is not made from spaces or font metrics. Like
+`%{X:size}`, it is scaled for the output.
+
 See **zelbar**(1) man page for more information.

 ### Output
